 of renewable energy technology</article-title><source>Energy Policy</source><year>2006</year><volume>34</volume><fpage>256</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.enpol.2004.08.029</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Scholz</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The POETICs of industrial carbon dioxide emissions in Japan: an urban and institutional extension of the IPAT identity</article-title><source>Carbon Balance and Management</source><year>2006</year><volume>1</volume><fpage>11</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17005049</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1186/1750-0680-1-11</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>S&#x000f6;derholm</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Ek</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Pettersson</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Wind power development in Sweden: Global policies and local obstacles</article-title><source>Renewable and Sustainable Energy Reviews</source><year>2007</year><volume>11</volume><fpage>365</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.rser.2005.03.001</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Nguyen</surname><given-names>KQ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Impacts of wind power generation and CO<sub>2 </sub>emission constraints on the future choice of fuels and technologies in the power sector of Vietnam</article-title><source>Energy Policy</source><year>2007</year><volume>35</volume><fpage>2305</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.enpol.2006.06.023</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lewis</surname><given-names>JI</g