ergy development in Tamil Nadu and Andhra Pradesh, India Institutional dynamics and barriers &#x02013; A case study</article-title><source>Energy Policy</source><year>2000</year><volume>28</volume><fpage>157</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0301-4215(00)00007-0</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Patel</surname><given-names>MR</given-names></name></person-group><source>Wind and Solar Power Systems</source><year>1999</year><publisher-name>CRC Press, New York</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B21"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Burton</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Sharpe</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Jenkins</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Bossanyi</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name></person-group><source>Wind Energy Handbook</source><year>2001</year><publisher-name>John Wiley &#x00026; Sons, New York</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B22"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Spera</surname><given-names>DA</given-names></name></person-group><source>Wind Turbine Technology: Fundamental Concepts of Wind Turbine Engineering</source><year>1994</year><volume>Chapter 9</volume><publisher-name>ASME Press: New York</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B23"><citation citation-type="other"><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.centreforenergy.com"/></citation></ref><ref id="B24"><citation citation-type="other"><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.windpowerindia.com"/></citation></ref><ref id="B25"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>MNES</collab></person-group><article-title>Annual Report: 2005&#x02013;06</article-title><source>Ministry of Non-conventional Energy Sources</source><year>2006</year><publisher-name>Govt. of India, New Delhi</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B26"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ramachandra</surname><given-names>TV</given-names></name><name><surname>Shruthi</surname><given-names>BV</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Wind energy potential mapping in Karnataka, India, using GIS</article-title><source>Energy Conversion and Management</source><year>2005</year><volume>46</volume><fpage>1561</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.enconman.2004.07.009</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B27"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>MNES</collab></person-group><article-title>Annual Report: 2004&#x02013;05</article-title><source>Ministry of Non-conventional Energy Sources</source><year>2005</year><publisher-name>Govt. of India, New Delhi</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B28"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Beurskens</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Jensen</surname><given-names>PH</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Economics of wind energy prospects and directions</article-title><source>Renewable Energy World</source><year>2001</year><volume>4</volume><fpage>103</fpage></citation></ref><ref id="B29"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Nouni</surname><given-names>MR</given-names></name><name><surname>Mullick</surname><given-names>SC</given-names></name><name><surname>Kandpal</surname><given-names>TC</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Techno-economics of small wind electric generator projects for decentralized power supply in India</article-title><source>Energy Policy</source><year>2007</year><volume>35</volume><fpage>2491</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.enpol.2006.08.011</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B30"><citation citation-ty